WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
- Speaking of summer,

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.790
there is also another name expected

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.990
to hit stages soon,

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.130
Menudo.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:05.963
That's right,

00:00:05.963 --> 00:00:06.930
the boy band is back
(audience claps)

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.600
as a reboot called,
"Menudo, A New Beginning".

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.430
And we've got the man behind the project

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.360
on the line right now.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.740
He is a friend of the show

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.710
and even stepped in as
for host for me once

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:17.543
when I was sick.

00:00:17.543 --> 00:00:18.376
So thank you.

00:00:18.376 --> 00:00:19.851
Say "Hi" to Mario Lopez everybody!

00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:23.970
(audience cheers)
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.920
What's up Mario?

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:26.753
- Hi Kelly,

00:00:26.753 --> 00:00:27.840
so nice to see you.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.310
Thank you so much for having me.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.510
- Absolutely. Always.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.670
Well, tell us about this Menudo revival

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.503
that you're working on.

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:34.620
This is cool.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.843
- I'm very excited about this.

00:00:35.843 --> 00:00:37.800
Menudo, for those who aren't familiar,

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.500
was an iconic boy band back in the day

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.230
before NSync, Backstreet Boys,

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.580
there's a picture right there.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.020
There's Ricky Martin on the end.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.160
He came from there.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.690
They've been around for decades.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.000
They were popular all over the world.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.833
Growing up,

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:52.666
I was a huge fan.

00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:53.499
You didn't see too many young

00:00:53.499 --> 00:00:55.320
Latino boy bands back in the day.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.670
But that's a beautiful thing about music,

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.503
as you know,

00:00:57.503 --> 00:00:58.800
it sort of transcends language,

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.790
culture, everything.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.623
And now,

00:01:00.623 --> 00:01:03.240
we're doing a fresh
re-imagination of the group

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.980
and it's been really exciting

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:05.940
to kind of put 'em together

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.340
and focus on this new direction.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.350
Still honoring the legacy of course,

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.820
of Menudo from back in the day.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.260
So we're gonna be very supportive

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.250
all the way around.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.960
- Ah, that's amazing to hear.
(audience cheers)

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.040
That's cool.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.020
You've been working on this
for like a year, right?

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.210
So how did you find the new members?

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.250
- Well, we started online, originally,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.200
and then had auditions literally

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.190
all over the country,

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.950
L.A., New York, Miami,

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.360
Puerto Rico even.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:31.290
And it was really hard

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.430
because it was so many great kids,

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.170
talented kids, to narrow it down

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.550
to our five favorites.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.630
But we ended up with a group

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.160
we really like.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.160
They're ages from like 10 to 14,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.960
so they're young, too.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:43.793
- Aw, that's cool!

00:01:43.793 --> 00:01:44.640
I love it, so cute!

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.230
So they have, the band
has a new single out.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.250
Tell us about it.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.159
- The new single is called, "Mi Amor".

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.120
They're coming out the gate strong,

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.650
just exceeded our expectations.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:53.483
They're great.

00:01:53.483 --> 00:01:54.930
We have some great producers

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:55.763
working with 'em

00:01:55.763 --> 00:01:56.596
and I can't wait for them

00:01:56.596 --> 00:01:57.570
to start performing

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.950
live all over the country.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.600
That's a, look at 'em right there.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.500
- [Kelly] So cute.
(audience claps)

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.690
- Very colorful in their outfits.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.680
Menudo mi amor!

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.539
It looks like they can all be my kids.

00:02:06.539 --> 00:02:07.372
(everyone laughs)

00:02:07.372 --> 00:02:08.490
- I love it.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.450
Thank you, Mario.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.680
It's always good to see you.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.030
Everybody, you heard it from him,

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:12.863
the new single,

00:02:12.863 --> 00:02:15.510
"Mi Amor" from "Menudo, A New Beginning",

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.790
is streaming on all platforms worldwide.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:18.623
Y'all gotta check it out.

00:02:18.623 --> 00:02:19.830
They're actually gonna be kicking off

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.840
their U.S. and international
tour this summer.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.190
Y'all gotta go get ready for that.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.060
It's gonna be a good time.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.170
We can see live shows, y'all,

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.003
remember COVID?

00:02:26.003 --> 00:02:26.836
It sucked.

00:02:26.836 --> 00:02:27.669
(audience claps)

00:02:27.669 --> 00:02:28.560
We can see live music again.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.393
Thank you Mario.

